cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite the associated peer-reviewed article
  when available and the versioned repository release used in your analysis.
title: >-
  SIC longitudinal multi-omics analysis: data-free reproducibility repository
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-25
authors:
  - family-names: Lyu
    given-names: Hao
repository-code: https://github.com/lvhao1123/SIC-longitudinal-multiomics
url: https://github.com/lvhao1123/SIC-longitudinal-multiomics
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, aggregate non-identifiable result tables, figure source data,
  quality-assurance outputs and software-environment records supporting a
  longitudinal transcriptomic and proteomic study of sepsis-induced
  coagulopathy. Participant-level CMAISE/OMIX011182 data are controlled access
  and are not redistributed.
keywords:
  - sepsis-induced coagulopathy
  - longitudinal multi-omics
  - transcriptomics
  - proteomics
  - survival analysis
  - reproducibility
